\cf4 \cb1 After implementing most of my design for the petri net, (I thought I had completed all of it, but I had not implemented passenger priority yet). I had Claude check to make sure the design was correct before I started applying it to code otherwise, I would have an incorrect design and incorrect code. I gave Claude the scenario, what needed to happen and my diagram which it then explained to me it had found a few errors. \
\'a0\
Firstly, I was outputting and inputting from the same transition connected to P3. This was a simple fix by creating another transition that output to P3. This was the same case to P11 which did have an input transition, only an output. I then changed the diagram to include an input transition as well.\
\'a0\
Secondly, t2 and t6 did not have any directional output when it was first implemented which was a mistake. It then told me I could the direction places that I had created between p4 and p3 for those transitions. I then added two arcs, one from p3 south to t2 and another from t7 to p7-exit North. It also mentioned t5 had no directional check, I then created a new place to check for this.
