\cf4 \cb1 I needed a way to see if a train from a given starting position and destination was actually reachable from each other. I did not know how to go about this so I asked Claude how I could do this. It responded with I could do a breadth first search (bfs) to see if the destination can be reached from the starting position. I was very familiar with a bfs, I had implemented it before so I knew it would not be too difficult to add, and it was something that was recently taught to us again in algorithms and data structures which was a good refresher. Because I had already created a bfs in a previous course I opened that code back up and used aspects of that to implement the new one. The great thing about the bfs is that it does not just calculate if the two positions meet each other but also reconstructs the route. Hence it is also used as a route for the trains which lets me know where they need to be moved to. \
