\cf4 \cb1 After uploading my code to Grade scope, I still had three tests that were not passing. After looking at the errors and the forum posts my code was missing two things.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf4 -
\f3 \'a0 
\f0 There was no priority check so a freight train going from 3-4 or 4-3 could move first instead of a passenger train at 6 or 1. \
-
\f3 \'a0  
\f0 If two trains are moving to the same section neither should move and it should result in a deadlock.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf4 I knew how to fix the first problem. I needed a condition that checks if a train is on either 3 or 4 and if there is a train either on 6 or 1. If there is a train on those sections the train on 3 and 4 cannot pass. The second problem however, I could not figure out, so I described it to Claude. It told me I needed to know where every train wanted to go before actually moving it and broke it down into three parts. \
	1. Work out where each train wants to go and record it\
	2. Count how many trains want to go into each section. If more than one train wants to go into a certain section, delete it so they don\'92t move\
	3. Move the trains \
